<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hanuman Chalisa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">16th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as हनुमान चालीसा, Hanumān Chālīsā</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Hanuman Chalisa, &quot;forty chaupais on Hanuman&quot;, is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> devotional hymn (stotra) in praise of Hanuman, written in Awadhi by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tulsidas">Tulsidas</a>, a poet-saint of the 16th century. Tulsidas, devoted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rama">Rama</a>, is best known for the Ramcharitmanas, his retelling of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramayana">Ramayana</a> in the Awadhi vernacular.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The <b>Hanuman Chalisa</b>, &quot;forty chaupais on Hanuman&quot;, is a Hindu devotional hymn (stotra) in praise of Hanuman, written in Awadhi by Tulsidas, a poet-saint of the 16th century.</blockquote><a href="/songs/hanuman-chalisa">Hanuman Chalisa</a></li></ul></section>
